#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063923 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9911dc0d-905d-54e1-aadb-f4fbce6f89d2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "75114520-8891-503c-81b7-be4c86f5d054" :question/math-academy-id "e-202" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y = \\arctan (-7x)$." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arctan x) = \\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\arctan (-7x)) \\\\\n&= (1)/(1 + (-7x)^{2}) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(-7x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{1 + 49x^{2}} \\cdot (-7) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{7}{1 + 49x^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063924 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c0a82f3e-9e04-50ce-b3b2-54fafd4c1db8" :question/math-academy-id "e-203" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$, if $y = \\arccos (5-8x)$." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arccos x) = -\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccos (5 - 8x)) \\\\\n&= - (1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (5 - 8x)^{2}}) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(5 - 8x) \\\\\n&= - (1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (25 - 80x + 64x^{2})}) \\cdot (-8) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80x - 24 - 64x^{2}}} \\\\\n&= (8)/(\\sqrt{4(20x - 6 - 16x^{2})}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{2\\sqrt{20x - 6 - 16x^{2}}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{20x - 6 - 16x^{2}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063925 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "0f8652d9-5d83-5d2c-93ae-2f3a4fc4e3e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-204" :question/problem "If $y= x \\arccos x$, calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "Applying the product rule and using the formula for the derivative of $\\arccos x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(x\\arccos x) &= x \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(\\arccos x) + \\arccos x\\frac{d}{dx}(x) \\\\\n&= x \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}) + \\arccos x \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}} + \\arccos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063926 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "552973a7-4ab5-5918-83f4-15ee0e3ee052" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/id #uuid "cbeacfa8-783e-5761-a74a-50b78a19ce20" :question/math-academy-id "e-206" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x) = 5\\arcsin(3x^2)$." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsin x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(5\\arcsin (3x^{2})) \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot (1)/(\\sqrt{1 - (3x^{2})^{2}}) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(3x^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1 - 9x^{4}}} \\cdot (6x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{30x}{\\sqrt{1 - 9x^{4}}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
